{# Body is a verbatim copy of the script wrapped in raw: it uses `${#x[@]}` (array length) throughout, which Jinja would read as a comment opener. Only the REPOS_DIR default is templated. Keep `-%}` on the raw tag or the shebang lands on line 2. #}
{% raw -%}
#!/usr/bin/env bash
# standing — start and tend a standing interactive Claude Code session in a
# Lentago repo, each in its own maximized terminal. Every session is one window
# of tmux session "lentago", named after its repo and holding one pane that
# runs `claude --name <repo>-standing` in that repo's checkout. Each window is
# viewed through its own grouped tmux session ("lentago-<repo>") with its own
# terminal, titled "<repo> — standing EM" at the terminal's normal font size, so
# a human finds a session by name in the window switcher and nothing runs hidden.
# Closing a terminal (or `standing hide <repo>`) only detaches a tmux client: the
# EM keeps running, and `standing show <repo>` brings its terminal back.
#
# Org model (see ~/repos/lentago/CLAUDE.md): the session at ~/repos/lentago is
# the Engineering Director; each standing session is that repo's Engineering
# Manager (EM), on Opus by default, free to spawn subagents of its own choice;
# Chris is Product Owner, CTO and CEO. EMs start on demand: the Director runs
# `standing up <repo> --director <its-name>` the first time a dispatch needs
# that EM, never for every repo at init, so a normal day grows from zero EMs
# to the handful it dispatches to.
#
# Dependencies: tmux (>= 3.2), claude, coreutils; ghostty/ptyxis/alacritty for `open`
#
# Usage:
#   standing                       same as `standing status`
#   standing up REPO [REPO ...]    start these EMs, a window and a terminal each —
#                                  idempotent: a running EM is left alone, a dead one is
#                                  respawned in place; a terminal opens only for an EM
#                                  this run starts or respawns, so one closed on purpose
#                                  stays closed (`open` fills them); others are not touched
#   standing up                    with no repos: every repo, in ORDER below (explicit use only)
#   standing up REPO --director NAME  tell the EM which session is its Director (NAME from
#                                  the "This session is …" line of ListAgents); remembered
#                                  for later up/restart calls — `--no-director` forgets it
#   standing up --no-open ...      don't open terminal windows
#   standing up --no-prompt ...    start claude at an empty prompt (no kickoff turn)
#   standing up --prompt 'text'    custom kickoff prompt
#   standing up kalmia -- --model opus   anything after `--` is passed to claude
#   standing restart [repo ...] [same flags as up]
#                                  /exit each pane and start a FRESH session in it (new model,
#                                  prompt, director); the EM's conversation and any in-flight
#                                  work are gone. Windows and terminals stay put. The Director
#                                  from the last --director is remembered on the tmux session,
#                                  so a bare `standing restart` keeps it.
#   standing down [repo ...]       send /exit, wait, then kill the EM's pane, window and
#                                  terminal; with no repos: every EM, then the tmux sessions
#   standing status                one row per EM: repo, state, terminal, pid, size, session
#                                  name (state "trust?" = waiting at Claude's folder-trust dialog)
#   standing trust [repo ...] [--yes]  list the EMs waiting at the folder-trust dialog and,
#                                  after a y/N prompt (or --yes), accept it in each — your
#                                  call to run; these are your repos and Claude won't run it for you
#   standing show REPO             open one maximized terminal on that EM's window, titled
#                                  "REPO — standing EM"; if a terminal already shows it, says
#                                  so and opens nothing
#   standing hide REPO             close that EM's terminal(s); its pane and claude keep running
#                                  (in a grid window, that terminal shows its neighbours too)
#   standing open                  open a maximized terminal for every EM window that has none,
#                                  including ones closed on purpose (`show REPO` opens just one)
#   standing attach [repo]         attach in *this* terminal (or switch-client inside tmux) to
#                                  the base session, which holds every EM window
#   standing tile                  re-apply the tiled layout (matters only with STANDING_PER_WINDOW > 1)
#   standing repos                 print the repo set a bare `up` would use, in ORDER
#
# Each terminal shows one EM; the tmux status line lists every EM window. To look
# across them from one terminal, `standing attach` and pick with prefix+w (Ctrl-b w).
# GNOME places new windows on the active monitor — Super+Shift+Arrow moves one.
#
# Environment:
#   STANDING_REPOS_DIR     where the clones live   (default: ~/repos/lentago)
#   STANDING_TMUX_SESSION  tmux session name       (default: lentago)
#   STANDING_PER_WINDOW    EMs per window          (default: 1 — a window and terminal each;
#                          N > 1 packs N tiled panes into windows standing-1, standing-2, …)
#   STANDING_MODEL         model every EM starts on (default: claude-opus-5-5; set it
#                          empty for Claude's own default; `-- --model X` overrides per run)
#   STANDING_NAME_SUFFIX   claude --name suffix    (default: standing → "kalmia-standing")
#   STANDING_TERMINAL      terminal for `open`     (default: first of ghostty, ptyxis, alacritty)
#   STANDING_FONT_SIZE     font size for those terminals only (ghostty/alacritty; default:
#                          unset, i.e. the terminal's own size)
#   STANDING_EXIT_WAIT     seconds `down`/`restart` wait after /exit before killing (default: 20)
#
# Notes:
#   * First launch in a repo Claude has never opened shows the folder-trust dialog
#     and waits there — `standing status` shows it as "trust?"; `standing trust` accepts.
#   * Panes keep remain-on-exit, so a crashed claude leaves its last screen
#     readable ("[dead]" on the border); `standing up` respawns it in place.
#   * Inherited CLAUDE* env vars are stripped from the children, so this can be
#     run from inside another Claude session without tripping nested-session guards.
#   * The base session "lentago" holds every EM window and remembers the Director;
#     window <repo> is viewed through "lentago-<repo>", one session group sharing
#     the windows. `down` with no repos removes them all.
#   * Windows standing-1, standing-2, … (the earlier tiled grid, or STANDING_PER_WINDOW
#     > 1) are still listed, restarted and downed; they are viewed through "lentago"
#     (N=1) and "lentago-vN" (N>1) as before.
#   * ANSIBLE MANAGED — kalmia roles/shell (like clean-all/pull-all). Local edits
#     are overwritten on the next run; change roles/shell/templates/standing.j2 instead.
set -euo pipefail

REPOS_DIR="${STANDING_REPOS_DIR:-{% endraw %}{{ repos_dir }}/lentago{% raw %}}"
TMUX_SESSION="${STANDING_TMUX_SESSION:-lentago}"
PER_WINDOW="${STANDING_PER_WINDOW:-1}"
MODEL="${STANDING_MODEL-claude-opus-5-5}"
NAME_SUFFIX="${STANDING_NAME_SUFFIX:-standing}"
EXIT_WAIT="${STANDING_EXIT_WAIT:-20}"
WIN_PREFIX="standing"   # grid windows: standing-1, standing-2, … (PER_WINDOW > 1, or older runs)
# Size a window has while no terminal is attached (so splits always fit);
# it follows the attached terminal's size afterwards.
DEF_W=320; DEF_H=100
# Field separator for tmux -F output: a tab is IFS whitespace and collapses when
# a field is empty (an untagged pane), shifting columns; this never does.
US=$'\x1f'

# Order a bare `standing up` starts repos in (and, with PER_WINDOW > 1, how they
# group into windows): platform first, then products/guides/sites, then the
# uvularia family. A repo not listed here comes after these, alphabetically.
ORDER=(
    claytonia drosera kalmia brasenia dotgithub betula solidago shared-workflows
    asclepias lupinus epigaea mitchella monarda osmunda site-lentago-dev site-icecreamtofightwith-com
    site-pondviewlane-com uvularia uvularia-records-template uvularia-rules-template
    uvularia-site-template uvularia-demo-records uvularia-demo-ask-rules uvularia-demo-site
)
# Never started: archived on GitHub, or a template nobody works in.
EXCLUDE=(coderabbit office-presence site-pitzilabs-dev workstation-bootstrap repo-template)

# Kickoff turn for each pane. %DIRECTOR% is replaced with the --director sentence (or nothing).
KICKOFF_DEFAULT='You are the Engineering Manager for this repo (see the org model in ~/repos/lentago/CLAUDE.md). %DIRECTOR%Chris is Product Owner, CTO and CEO. You may spawn subagents of your own choice (Haiku, Sonnet, Opus) for parallel or read-only work; their judgments come back through you. Introduce yourself per your CLAUDE.md, call ListAgents once so you know your peers, then stand by. Do not start any work until asked.'
# shellcheck disable=SC2016  # backticks are markdown in the prompt, not a command
DIRECTOR_SENTENCE='Your Engineering Director is the session named `%NAME%`; report to it with SendMessage when work is done or blocked. '

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- helpers ----

c_ok=$'\033[0;32m'; c_warn=$'\033[1;33m'; c_err=$'\033[1;31m'; c_dim=$'\033[2m'; c_off=$'\033[0m'
say()  { printf '%s\n' "$*"; }
ok()   { printf '%s  ✓%s %s\n' "$c_ok" "$c_off" "$*"; }
warn() { printf '%s  ⚠ %s%s\n' "$c_warn" "$*" "$c_off" >&2; }
die()  { printf '%sstanding: %s%s\n' "$c_err" "$*" "$c_off" >&2; exit 1; }

need() { command -v "$1" >/dev/null 2>&1 || die "$1 not found on PATH"; }

# Strip every CLAUDE* variable from our own environment so a tmux server we
# start does not carry a parent session's identity into the children.
# (Hence no script variable may start with CLAUDE — e.g. CLI_BIN, not CLAUDE_BIN.)
scrub_env() {
    local v
    while IFS= read -r v; do unset "$v"; done < <(compgen -v | grep -E '^CLAUDE' || true)
}

has_session() { tmux has-session -t "=$TMUX_SESSION" 2>/dev/null; }

# Standing windows, in window order: every window this script made (tagged
# @standing) plus grid windows standing-N from runs before the tag existed.
std_windows() {
    has_session || return 0
    tmux list-windows -t "=$TMUX_SESSION" -F "#{window_name}${US}#{@standing}" 2>/dev/null \
        | awk -F"$US" -v p="^${WIN_PREFIX}-[0-9]+$" '$2 == 1 || $1 ~ p { print $1 }' || true
}
# The grid windows among them (standing-1, standing-2, …), in numeric order.
grid_windows() { std_windows | grep -E "^${WIN_PREFIX}-[0-9]+$" | sort -t- -k2,2n || true; }
is_grid()   { [[ "$1" =~ ^${WIN_PREFIX}-[0-9]+$ ]]; }
# A repo's own window is named after it; tmux reads '.' and ':' in a target as
# separators, so those become '_'. A repo named like a grid window (standing-N)
# or its view (vN, as in "lentago-vN") gets a leading '_', so neither collides.
win_name() {
    local n=${1//[.:]/_}
    [[ "$n" =~ ^(v|${WIN_PREFIX}-)[0-9]+$ ]] && n="_$n"
    printf '%s' "$n"
}
win_t()     { printf '=%s:=%s' "$TMUX_SESSION" "$1"; }              # exact window target
win_num()   { printf '%s' "${1##*-}"; }
win_panes() { tmux list-panes -t "$(win_t "$1")" -F '#{pane_id}' 2>/dev/null | wc -l; }
# The grouped session through which a window is viewed: "lentago-<repo>" for a
# repo's own window; for grid window N, the base session (N=1) or "lentago-vN".
view_for() {
    if is_grid "$1"; then
        local n; n=$(win_num "$1")
        (( n == 1 )) && printf '%s' "$TMUX_SESSION" || printf '%s-v%s' "$TMUX_SESSION" "$n"
    else
        printf '%s-%s' "$TMUX_SESSION" "$1"
    fi
}
# The inverse, from a view session's name; empty for the base session.
view_window() {
    [[ "$1" == "$TMUX_SESSION"-* ]] || return 0
    local rest=${1#"$TMUX_SESSION"-}
    if [[ "$rest" =~ ^v([0-9]+)$ ]]; then printf '%s-%s' "$WIN_PREFIX" "${BASH_REMATCH[1]}"; else printf '%s' "$rest"; fi
}
# The base session and every session grouped with it. Matched on the group, not
# on a name prefix, so another standing session ("lentago-test") is never caught.
view_sessions() {
    tmux list-sessions -F "#{session_name}${US}#{session_group}" 2>/dev/null \
        | awk -F"$US" -v s="$TMUX_SESSION" '$1 == s || $2 == s { print $1 }' || true
}
# Terminals attached to a session; 0 when the session doesn't exist yet (an EM
# started with --no-open has no view), which under pipefail must not fail.
clients_of() { { tmux list-clients -t "=$1" 2>/dev/null || true; } | wc -l; }

# window US pane_id US repo for every pane in every standing window.
all_panes() {
    has_session || return 0
    tmux list-panes -s -t "=$TMUX_SESSION" -F "#{window_name}${US}#{pane_id}${US}#{@repo}${US}#{@standing}" 2>/dev/null \
        | awk -F"$US" -v OFS="$US" -v p="^${WIN_PREFIX}-[0-9]+$" '$4 == 1 || $1 ~ p { print $1, $2, $3 }' || true
}
pane_for()    { all_panes | awk -F"$US" -v r="$1" '$3 == r { print $2; exit }'; }
window_of()   { all_panes | awk -F"$US" -v id="$1" '$2 == id { print $1; exit }'; }
pane_dead()   { [[ "$(tmux display-message -p -t "$1" '#{pane_dead}' 2>/dev/null)" == 1 ]]; }
pane_exists() { tmux display-message -p -t "$1" '#{pane_id}' >/dev/null 2>&1; }
# Claude's first-run folder-trust dialog is on screen: both options as whole
# lines plus the confirm hint, so a pane merely quoting the sentence doesn't match.
at_trust_prompt() {
    local screen
    screen=$(tmux capture-pane -p -t "$1" 2>/dev/null) || return 1
    grep -qE '^ *(❯ +)?No, exit *$' <<<"$screen" \
        && grep -qE '^ *(❯ +)?Yes, I trust this folder *$' <<<"$screen" \
        && grep -qF 'Enter to confirm' <<<"$screen"
}
trust_cursor_on_yes() { tmux capture-pane -p -t "$1" 2>/dev/null | grep -qE '^ *❯ +Yes, I trust this folder *$'; }

in_exclude() { local r; for r in "${EXCLUDE[@]}"; do [[ "$r" == "$1" ]] && return 0; done; return 1; }

# Every git clone under REPOS_DIR minus EXCLUDE, in ORDER (unknowns last, sorted).
all_repos() {
    local -A have=()
    local d n r
    for d in "$REPOS_DIR"/*/; do
        [[ -d "$d/.git" ]] || continue
        n=$(basename "$d")
        in_exclude "$n" || have[$n]=1
    done
    for r in "${ORDER[@]}"; do
        [[ -n "${have[$r]:-}" ]] || continue
        printf '%s\n' "$r"; unset "have[$r]"
    done
    (( ${#have[@]} == 0 )) || printf '%s\n' "${!have[@]}" | sort
}

# Populate REPOS from args: explicit names, or everything.
resolve_repos() {
    local r
    REPOS=()
    for r in "$@"; do
        case "$r" in
            --all) ;;                      # accepted for old habits; it is the default
            -*)    die "unknown option: $r" ;;
            *)     REPOS+=("$r") ;;
        esac
    done
    (( ${#REPOS[@]} )) || mapfile -t REPOS < <(all_repos)
    for r in "${REPOS[@]}"; do
        [[ -d "$REPOS_DIR/$r/.git" ]] || die "$REPOS_DIR/$r is not a git checkout"
    done
}

# The Director's session name is remembered on the base tmux session so later
# `up`/`restart` calls without --director keep pointing the EMs at it.
remember_director() { has_session && tmux set-option -t "$TMUX_SESSION:" @director "$1" 2>/dev/null || true; }
forget_director()   { has_session && tmux set-option -qu -t "$TMUX_SESSION:" @director 2>/dev/null || true; }
recall_director()   { has_session && tmux show-options -qv -t "$TMUX_SESSION:" @director 2>/dev/null || true; }

# Flags shared by `up` and `restart`: sets PROMPT, USE_PROMPT, OPEN, DIRECTOR,
# SEL (repo names) and EXTRA (args after --). DIRECTOR falls back to the
# remembered one; call remember_director after the session exists.
parse_launch_flags() {
    PROMPT="$KICKOFF_DEFAULT"; USE_PROMPT=1; OPEN=1; DIRECTOR=""; NO_DIRECTOR=0; SEL=(); EXTRA=()
    while (( $# )); do
        case "$1" in
            --no-prompt)  USE_PROMPT=0; shift ;;
            --no-director) NO_DIRECTOR=1; shift ;;
            --no-open)    OPEN=0; shift ;;
            --director)   [[ $# -ge 2 ]] || die "--director needs a session name"; DIRECTOR=$2; shift 2 ;;
            --director=*) DIRECTOR=${1#--director=}; shift ;;
            --prompt)     [[ $# -ge 2 ]] || die "--prompt needs a value"; PROMPT=$2; shift 2 ;;
            --prompt=*)   PROMPT=${1#--prompt=}; shift ;;
            --)           shift; EXTRA=("$@"); break ;;
            *)            SEL+=("$1"); shift ;;
        esac
    done
    if (( NO_DIRECTOR )); then
        DIRECTOR=""
    elif [[ -z "$DIRECTOR" ]]; then
        DIRECTOR=$(recall_director)
    fi
    local dsent=""
    [[ -n "$DIRECTOR" ]] && dsent=${DIRECTOR_SENTENCE//%NAME%/$DIRECTOR}
    PROMPT=${PROMPT//%DIRECTOR%/$dsent}
}

# Build the argv that runs claude in a pane: CLAUDE* stripped from the tmux
# server's global environment too (it may predate this script), the default
# model unless the caller passed one, then the caller's extras and the prompt.
# Prints NUL-separated.
claude_argv() {
    local repo=$1; shift
    local -a cmd=(env)
    local v a has_model=0
    while IFS= read -r v; do cmd+=(-u "$v"); done \
        < <(tmux show-environment -g 2>/dev/null | grep -oE '^CLAUDE[A-Za-z0-9_]*' || true)
    cmd+=("$CLI_BIN" --name "$repo-$NAME_SUFFIX")
    for a in "${EXTRA[@]}"; do [[ "$a" == --model || "$a" == --model=* ]] && has_model=1; done
    [[ -n "$MODEL" && $has_model == 0 ]] && cmd+=(--model "$MODEL")
    cmd+=("${EXTRA[@]}")
    (( USE_PROMPT )) && cmd+=("$PROMPT")
    printf '%s\0' "${cmd[@]}"
}

# Create the pane for a repo (creating the session as needed); prints its id.
# PER_WINDOW 1: a new window named after the repo. PER_WINDOW > 1: the first
# grid window with room, else the next grid window standing-N.
spawn_pane() {
    local repo=$1 dir=$2; shift 2
    local id w name target="" last n
    if (( PER_WINDOW == 1 )); then
        name=$(win_name "$repo")
    else
        for w in $(grid_windows); do
            if (( $(win_panes "$w") < PER_WINDOW )); then target=$w; break; fi
        done
        last=$(grid_windows | tail -n1)
        n=1; [[ -n "$last" ]] && n=$(( $(win_num "$last") + 1 ))
        name="$WIN_PREFIX-$n"
    fi
    if [[ -n "$target" ]]; then
        id=$(tmux split-window -d -P -F '#{pane_id}' -t "$(win_t "$target")" -c "$dir" -- "$@")
    elif ! has_session; then
        id=$(tmux new-session -d -P -F '#{pane_id}' -s "$TMUX_SESSION" -n "$name" \
                -x "$DEF_W" -y "$DEF_H" -c "$dir" -- "$@")
    else
        id=$(tmux new-window -d -P -F '#{pane_id}' -t "=$TMUX_SESSION:" -n "$name" -c "$dir" -- "$@")
    fi
    tmux set-option -w -t "$id" @standing 1
    tmux set-option -p -t "$id" @repo "$repo"
    printf '%s' "$id"
}

# Escape clears any dialog or half-typed input, then a clean /exit; waits up to
# EXIT_WAIT seconds for the pane to die (SessionEnd hooks run that way).
graceful_exit() {
    local id=$1 repo=$2 i
    pane_dead "$id" && return 0
    tmux send-keys -t "$id" Escape
    sleep 0.3
    tmux send-keys -t "$id" '/exit' Enter
    for (( i = 0; i < EXIT_WAIT * 2; i++ )); do
        pane_exists "$id" || return 0
        pane_dead "$id" && return 0
        sleep 0.5
    done
    warn "$repo did not exit within ${EXIT_WAIT}s — killing"
    return 1
}

# Idempotent settings on every standing window and view session: labelled
# borders, dead panes kept, mouse, size that follows the attached terminal.
apply_options() {
    local w s
    for s in $(view_sessions); do
        tmux set-option -t "$s:" default-size "${DEF_W}x${DEF_H}"
        tmux set-option -t "$s:" mouse on
    done
    for w in $(std_windows); do
        tmux set-option -w -t "$(win_t "$w")" window-size latest
        tmux set-option -w -t "$(win_t "$w")" automatic-rename off
        tmux set-option -w -t "$(win_t "$w")" remain-on-exit on
        tmux set-option -w -t "$(win_t "$w")" pane-border-status top
        tmux set-option -w -t "$(win_t "$w")" pane-border-format ' #{@repo}#{?pane_dead, [dead],} '
        tmux select-layout -t "$(win_t "$w")" tiled >/dev/null
    done
}

have_display() { [[ -n "${DISPLAY:-}${WAYLAND_DISPLAY:-}" ]]; }

pick_terminal() {
    local t
    TERM_BIN="${STANDING_TERMINAL:-}"
    [[ -n "$TERM_BIN" ]] && return 0
    for t in ghostty ptyxis alacritty; do
        command -v "$t" >/dev/null 2>&1 && { TERM_BIN=$t; return 0; }
    done
    die "no terminal emulator found (ghostty, ptyxis, alacritty) — set STANDING_TERMINAL"
}

# A terminal's title: "<repo> — standing EM" for an EM's own window, the window
# name for a grid window, which holds several.
term_title() {
    local repo
    if is_grid "$1"; then printf '%s' "$1"; return 0; fi
    repo=$(tmux display-message -p -t "$(win_t "$1")" '#{@repo}' 2>/dev/null || true)
    printf '%s — standing EM' "${repo:-$1}"
}

# Open a maximized terminal attached to a view session, with the given title,
# at the terminal's own font size unless STANDING_FONT_SIZE says otherwise.
launch_terminal() {
    local view=$1 title=$2 fs="${STANDING_FONT_SIZE:-}"
    local -a attach=(tmux attach-session -t "=$view") cmd
    case "$TERM_BIN" in
        ghostty)   cmd=(ghostty --maximize=true --title="$title" ${fs:+--font-size="$fs"} -e "${attach[@]}") ;;
        ptyxis)    cmd=(ptyxis --new-window --maximize --title "$title" -- "${attach[@]}") ;;
        alacritty) cmd=(alacritty --title "$title" -o window.startup_mode=Maximized ${fs:+-o font.size="$fs"} -e "${attach[@]}") ;;
        *)         cmd=("$TERM_BIN" -e "${attach[@]}") ;;
    esac
    setsid -f "${cmd[@]}" >/dev/null 2>&1
}

# Remove view sessions whose window no longer exists (closes their terminals) —
# left behind when a pane was closed by hand, say, and now showing another EM.
prune_views() {
    local s w
    local -a wins=()
    mapfile -t wins < <(tmux list-windows -t "=$TMUX_SESSION" -F '#{window_name}' 2>/dev/null || true)
    for s in $(view_sessions); do
        w=$(view_window "$s")
        [[ -n "$w" ]] || continue
        printf '%s\n' "${wins[@]}" | grep -qxF -- "$w" || tmux kill-session -t "=$s" 2>/dev/null || true
    done
}

# Close the terminal showing a window that is about to go: kill its view
# session, or for grid window 1 (viewed through the base session, which must
# stay) detach the base session's clients.
close_view() {
    local view; view=$(view_for "$1")
    if [[ "$view" == "$TMUX_SESSION" ]]; then
        tmux detach-client -s "=$TMUX_SESSION" 2>/dev/null || true
    else
        tmux kill-session -t "=$view" 2>/dev/null || true
    fi
}

# ------------------------------------------------------------- commands ----

cmd_up() {
    need tmux; need claude
    [[ "$PER_WINDOW" =~ ^[1-9][0-9]*$ ]] || die "STANDING_PER_WINDOW must be a positive integer, not '$PER_WINDOW'"
    CLI_BIN=$(command -v claude)
    parse_launch_flags "$@"
    resolve_repos "${SEL[@]}"
    scrub_env

    local repo dir id w where started=0 respawned=0 kept=0
    local -a want=()   # windows of the EMs this run starts or respawns: the only ones it opens
    for repo in "${REPOS[@]}"; do
        dir="$REPOS_DIR/$repo"
        local -a cmd=()
        mapfile -d '' cmd < <(claude_argv "$repo")
        (( ${#cmd[@]} >= 3 )) || die "internal: could not build the claude command for $repo"

        id=$(pane_for "$repo")
        if [[ -n "$id" ]]; then
            if pane_dead "$id"; then
                tmux respawn-pane -k -t "$id" -c "$dir" -- "${cmd[@]}"
                want+=("$(window_of "$id")")
                ok "$repo respawned"
                respawned=$((respawned + 1))
            else
                say "${c_dim}  · $repo already running${c_off}"
                kept=$((kept + 1))
            fi
        else
            id=$(spawn_pane "$repo" "$dir" "${cmd[@]}")
            w=$(window_of "$id"); want+=("$w")
            if [[ "$w" == "$(win_name "$repo")" ]]; then where="its own window"; else where="window $w"; fi
            ok "$repo started in $where  ${c_dim}(claude --name $repo-$NAME_SUFFIX${MODEL:+ --model $MODEL})${c_off}"
            started=$((started + 1))
        fi
        apply_options
    done
    if (( NO_DIRECTOR )); then forget_director; elif [[ -n "$DIRECTOR" ]]; then remember_director "$DIRECTOR"; fi
    say ""
    say "Up: $started started, $respawned respawned, $kept already running, $(std_windows | wc -l) window(s)${DIRECTOR:+, Director $DIRECTOR}"
    # Terminals only for what this run started: a window whose terminal someone
    # closed on purpose stays closed until an explicit `standing open`.
    local -A asked=()
    if (( OPEN )) && have_display && (( ${#want[@]} )); then
        open_terminals "${want[@]}"
        for w in "${want[@]}"; do asked[$w]=1; done
    fi
    local lacking=0
    for w in $(std_windows); do
        [[ -n "${asked[$w]:-}" ]] && continue
        if (( $(clients_of "$(view_for "$w")") == 0 )); then lacking=$((lacking + 1)); fi
    done
    if (( lacking )); then
        say "$lacking window(s) without a terminal, left as they are: 'standing open' opens them, 'standing attach' looks in"
    fi
}

cmd_restart() {
    need tmux; need claude
    CLI_BIN=$(command -v claude)
    parse_launch_flags "$@"
    has_session || die "tmux session '$TMUX_SESSION' is not running — 'standing up' first"
    local -a targets=()
    if (( ${#SEL[@]} )); then
        targets=("${SEL[@]}")
    else
        mapfile -t targets < <(all_panes | awk -F"$US" '$3 != "" { print $3 }')
    fi
    scrub_env
    local repo id n=0
    for repo in "${targets[@]}"; do
        id=$(pane_for "$repo")
        [[ -n "$id" ]] || { warn "$repo: no such pane"; continue; }
        local -a cmd=()
        mapfile -d '' cmd < <(claude_argv "$repo")
        (( ${#cmd[@]} >= 3 )) || die "internal: could not build the claude command for $repo"
        graceful_exit "$id" "$repo" || true
        tmux respawn-pane -k -t "$id" -c "$REPOS_DIR/$repo" -- "${cmd[@]}"
        ok "$repo restarted  ${c_dim}(${MODEL:+--model $MODEL})${c_off}"
        n=$((n + 1))
    done
    apply_options
    if (( NO_DIRECTOR )); then forget_director; elif [[ -n "$DIRECTOR" ]]; then remember_director "$DIRECTOR"; fi
    say ""
    say "Restarted $n pane(s) in place as fresh sessions${DIRECTOR:+, Director $DIRECTOR}"
}

# One row per EM, in window order. TERM is how many terminals show the EM's
# window ("none" — 'standing open' fixes it); WINDOW appears only while some EM
# sits in a window not named after it (a grid window standing-N).
cmd_status() {
    need tmux
    if ! has_session || [[ -z "$(std_windows)" ]]; then
        say "tmux session '$TMUX_SESSION' is not running — 'standing up <repo>' starts an EM"
        return 0
    fi
    local w n term id repo dead pid cmdname size state i show_win=0 lacking=0
    local -a r_repo=() r_state=() r_term=() r_win=() r_pid=() r_size=()
    for w in $(std_windows); do
        n=$(clients_of "$(view_for "$w")")
        if (( n == 0 )); then term=none; lacking=$((lacking + 1)); else term=$n; fi
        while IFS="$US" read -r id repo dead pid cmdname size; do
            [[ -n "$repo" ]] || repo="(untagged $id)"
            if [[ "$dead" == 1 ]]; then
                state="${c_err}dead${c_off}"
            elif [[ "$cmdname" == claude* || "$cmdname" == node* ]] && at_trust_prompt "$id"; then
                state="${c_warn}trust?${c_off}"
            elif [[ "$cmdname" == claude* || "$cmdname" == node* ]]; then
                state="${c_ok}running${c_off}"
            else
                state="${c_warn}$cmdname${c_off}"
            fi
            [[ "$w" == "$(win_name "$repo")" ]] || show_win=1
            r_repo+=("$repo"); r_state+=("$state"); r_term+=("$term"); r_win+=("$w"); r_pid+=("$pid"); r_size+=("$size")
        done < <(tmux list-panes -t "$(win_t "$w")" -F "#{pane_id}${US}#{@repo}${US}#{pane_dead}${US}#{pane_pid}${US}#{pane_current_command}${US}#{pane_width}x#{pane_height}")
    done
    if (( show_win )); then
        printf '%-30s %-9s %-5s %-12s %-8s %-9s %s\n' REPO STATE TERM WINDOW PID SIZE SESSION
    else
        printf '%-30s %-9s %-5s %-8s %-9s %s\n' REPO STATE TERM PID SIZE SESSION
    fi
    for i in "${!r_repo[@]}"; do
        # %-20b: the state carries 11 bytes of colour codes, so it pads to 9 visible.
        if (( show_win )); then
            printf '%-30s %-20b %-5s %-12s %-8s %-9s %s\n' "${r_repo[$i]}" "${r_state[$i]}" "${r_term[$i]}" \
                "${r_win[$i]}" "${r_pid[$i]}" "${r_size[$i]}" "${r_repo[$i]}-$NAME_SUFFIX"
        else
            printf '%-30s %-20b %-5s %-8s %-9s %s\n' "${r_repo[$i]}" "${r_state[$i]}" "${r_term[$i]}" \
                "${r_pid[$i]}" "${r_size[$i]}" "${r_repo[$i]}-$NAME_SUFFIX"
        fi
    done
    if (( lacking )); then
        say "${c_warn}$lacking window(s) without a terminal — 'standing open' opens them${c_off}"
    fi
}

cmd_down() {
    need tmux
    has_session || { say "tmux session '$TMUX_SESSION' is not running"; return 0; }
    local -a targets=()
    local whole=0
    if (( $# )); then
        targets=("$@")
    else
        whole=1
        mapfile -t targets < <(all_panes | awk -F"$US" '$3 != "" { print $3 }')
    fi
    local repo id w
    for repo in "${targets[@]}"; do
        id=$(pane_for "$repo")
        [[ -n "$id" ]] || { warn "$repo: no such pane"; continue; }
        w=$(window_of "$id")
        graceful_exit "$id" "$repo" || true
        # The window goes with its last pane: close its terminal first, so it
        # never flashes another EM's window on the way out.
        if (( $(win_panes "$w") <= 1 )); then close_view "$w"; fi
        pane_exists "$id" && tmux kill-pane -t "$id"
        ok "$repo down"
        if (( ! whole )) && tmux list-windows -t "=$TMUX_SESSION" -F '#{window_name}' 2>/dev/null | grep -qxF "$w"; then
            tmux select-layout -t "$(win_t "$w")" tiled >/dev/null
        fi
    done
    if (( whole )); then
        local s
        for s in $(view_sessions); do
            [[ "$s" == "$TMUX_SESSION" ]] || tmux kill-session -t "=$s" 2>/dev/null || true
        done
        has_session && tmux kill-session -t "=$TMUX_SESSION"
        ok "tmux session '$TMUX_SESSION' closed"
    else
        prune_views
    fi
}

cmd_open() { open_terminals; }

# Open a maximized terminal for each named window that has none: every standing
# window when none are named (`standing open`); `up` names only the windows of
# the EMs it just started or respawned.
open_terminals() {
    need tmux
    has_session || die "tmux session '$TMUX_SESSION' is not running — 'standing up' first"
    local w view all=0
    local -a wins=("$@") missing=()
    local -A seen=()
    prune_views
    if (( ${#wins[@]} == 0 )); then all=1; mapfile -t wins < <(std_windows); fi
    # Views first (cheap, no display needed), then decide whether a terminal is even wanted.
    for w in "${wins[@]}"; do
        [[ -z "${seen[$w]:-}" ]] || continue   # two EMs started into one grid window
        seen[$w]=1
        view=$(view_for "$w")
        if ! tmux has-session -t "=$view" 2>/dev/null; then
            # A grouped session: same windows as the base, its own current window.
            tmux new-session -d -t "$TMUX_SESSION" -s "$view"
        fi
        tmux select-window -t "=$view:=$w"
        if (( $(clients_of "$view") == 0 )); then missing+=("$w"); fi
    done
    apply_options
    if (( ${#missing[@]} == 0 )); then
        if (( all )); then say "Every window already has a terminal"; else say "Already in a terminal: ${!seen[*]}"; fi
        return 0
    fi
    have_display || die "no display — use 'standing attach' from a terminal instead"
    pick_terminal
    scrub_env
    for w in "${missing[@]}"; do
        launch_terminal "$(view_for "$w")" "$(term_title "$w")"
        ok "opened $TERM_BIN for $w"
    done
    # Re-tile grid windows once the new clients' sizes have been picked up
    # (a window of one pane has nothing to tile).
    if [[ -n "$(grid_windows)" ]]; then
        ( sleep 2; for w in $(grid_windows); do tmux select-layout -t "$(win_t "$w")" tiled >/dev/null 2>&1; done ) &
    fi
}

# One EM's terminal: open it unless a terminal already shows that EM's window.
cmd_show() {
    need tmux
    if (( $# != 1 )) || [[ "$1" == -* ]]; then die "usage: standing show <repo>"; fi
    local repo=$1 id w n
    id=$(pane_for "$repo")
    [[ -n "$id" ]] || die "$repo has no standing EM — 'standing up $repo' starts one, terminal included"
    w=$(window_of "$id")
    tmux select-pane -t "$id"   # in a grid window, focus this EM's pane
    n=$(clients_of "$(view_for "$w")")
    if (( n )); then
        say "$repo is already shown in $n terminal(s)"
        return 0
    fi
    open_terminals "$w"
}

# Close one EM's terminal(s) by detaching every client of its view session; the
# pane and its claude keep running, and `standing show <repo>` brings one back.
cmd_hide() {
    need tmux
    if (( $# != 1 )) || [[ "$1" == -* ]]; then die "usage: standing hide <repo>"; fi
    local repo=$1 id view n
    id=$(pane_for "$repo")
    [[ -n "$id" ]] || die "$repo has no standing EM ('standing status' lists them)"
    view=$(view_for "$(window_of "$id")")
    n=$(clients_of "$view")
    if (( n == 0 )); then
        say "$repo has no terminal open; its session keeps running"
        return 0
    fi
    tmux detach-client -s "=$view"
    ok "closed $n terminal(s) for $repo; its session keeps running"
}

cmd_attach() {
    need tmux
    has_session || die "tmux session '$TMUX_SESSION' is not running — 'standing up' first"
    if (( $# )); then
        local id w; id=$(pane_for "$1")
        [[ -n "$id" ]] || die "$1: no such pane"
        w=$(window_of "$id")
        tmux select-window -t "$(win_t "$w")"
        tmux select-pane -t "$id"
    fi
    if [[ -n "${TMUX:-}" ]]; then
        tmux switch-client -t "=$TMUX_SESSION"
    else
        exec tmux attach-session -t "=$TMUX_SESSION"
    fi
}

cmd_trust() {
    need tmux
    [[ -n "$(std_windows)" ]] || die "no standing windows in session '$TMUX_SESSION'"
    local yes=0 a w id repo lbl i n=0
    local -a only=() w_ids=() w_repos=() w_wins=()
    for a in "$@"; do
        case "$a" in
            --yes|-y) yes=1 ;;
            -*)       die "unknown option: $a" ;;
            *)        only+=("$a") ;;
        esac
    done
    while IFS="$US" read -r w id repo; do
        if (( ${#only[@]} )); then
            local hit=0; for a in "${only[@]}"; do [[ "$a" == "$repo" ]] && hit=1; done
            (( hit )) || continue
        fi
        at_trust_prompt "$id" || continue
        w_ids+=("$id"); w_repos+=("$repo"); w_wins+=("$w")
    done < <(all_panes)
    if (( ${#w_ids[@]} == 0 )); then
        say "No pane is waiting at the folder-trust dialog"
        return 0
    fi
    say "Waiting at the folder-trust dialog:"
    for i in "${!w_ids[@]}"; do
        w=${w_wins[$i]}
        if [[ "$w" == "$(win_name "${w_repos[$i]}")" ]]; then w=""; else w="  ${c_dim}($w)${c_off}"; fi
        say "  ${w_repos[$i]}$w"
    done
    if (( ! yes )); then
        [[ -t 0 ]] || die "not a terminal — pass --yes to accept without the prompt"
        read -r -p "Accept folder trust in these ${#w_ids[@]} pane(s)? [y/N] " a
        [[ "$a" =~ ^[Yy] ]] || { say "Nothing accepted"; return 0; }
    fi
    for i in "${!w_ids[@]}"; do
        id=${w_ids[$i]}; repo=${w_repos[$i]}; w=${w_wins[$i]}
        lbl=$repo; [[ "$w" == "$(win_name "$repo")" ]] || lbl+=" ($w)"
        at_trust_prompt "$id" || { warn "$lbl: dialog gone, skipped"; continue; }
        # Move the cursor onto "Yes" unless it is already there, let the dialog
        # redraw, and only confirm once the cursor is verifiably on Yes — a Down
        # that arrives before the dialog reads keys echoes as text instead.
        trust_cursor_on_yes "$id" || { tmux send-keys -t "$id" Down; sleep 0.6; }
        if trust_cursor_on_yes "$id"; then
            tmux send-keys -t "$id" Enter
            # Give the dialog up to 5 s to go away before calling it a failure.
            for (( a = 0; a < 10; a++ )); do
                sleep 0.5
                pane_dead "$id" && break
                at_trust_prompt "$id" || break
            done
            if pane_dead "$id"; then
                warn "$lbl: claude exited instead of accepting — 'standing up' respawns it"
            elif at_trust_prompt "$id"; then
                warn "$lbl: the dialog is still showing — click the pane and accept by hand"
            else
                ok "$lbl: accepted folder trust"
                n=$((n + 1))
            fi
        else
            warn "$lbl: cursor is not on Yes — click the pane and accept by hand"
        fi
    done
    say "Accepted in $n pane(s)"
}

cmd_tile() {
    need tmux
    [[ -n "$(std_windows)" ]] || die "no standing windows in session '$TMUX_SESSION'"
    apply_options
    ok "tiled $(all_panes | wc -l) panes across $(std_windows | wc -l) window(s)"
}

cmd_repos() {
    resolve_repos "$@"
    printf '%s\n' "${REPOS[@]}"
}

usage() { sed -n '2,/^set -euo/{/^set -euo/d;s/^# \{0,1\}//;p}' "$0"; }

main() {
    local sub=${1:-status}
    (( $# )) && shift
    case "$sub" in
        up)             cmd_up "$@" ;;
        restart)        cmd_restart "$@" ;;
        down|stop)      cmd_down "$@" ;;
        status|ls)      cmd_status "$@" ;;
        open)           cmd_open "$@" ;;
        show)           cmd_show "$@" ;;
        hide)           cmd_hide "$@" ;;
        attach|a)       cmd_attach "$@" ;;
        tile)           cmd_tile "$@" ;;
        trust)          cmd_trust "$@" ;;
        repos)          cmd_repos "$@" ;;
        -h|--help|help) usage ;;
        *)              die "unknown command: $sub (try --help)" ;;
    esac
}

main "$@"
{% endraw %}
